# "Target attacking creature" is any attacking creature, and the granted ability belongs to that creature, so its controller
# controls the trigger (CR 603.3a) and picks the artifact. On turn four Bot2's Ornithopter attacks Bot1; Bot1 casts the Ire
# on it (Bot1's own pump hurts: a 2/4 flyer deals 2), and when it connects Bot2, not Bot1, chooses the target artifact
# Bot1 controls - the Mox Pearl rather than the Mox Ruby.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Plains x3
Dreadmaw's Ire
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Attackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dreadmaw's Ire.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Pearl; Dreadmaw's Ire
